TITLE:: Insight
summary:: a sound engineer's window on a bus: spectrum, loudness, true peak, image
categories:: Libraries>Insight
related:: Classes/InsightLoudness, Classes/InsightSpectrum, Classes/BusManager, Classes/Bus

DESCRIPTION::
Point it at a bus - by index, by strong::BusManager:: name, by link::Classes/Bus::, or at a module - and it shows what a mastering chain wants to know: the spectrum, the levels with true peak, loudness the way EBU R128 means it, and the stereo image. One synth does the per-sample work and the window draws what it finds.

code::
s.boot;
Insight(\main, 0, 2);          // bus 0, two channels: the main out
Insight.at(\main).gui;         // the window

Insight.open;                  // or, in one line, on the main out
::

Everything you reach it by is on the class: there is one insight per name, the way there is one server, and code::Insight.at:: looks a name up again from anywhere. Nothing is ever allocated on the bus it watches and nothing is freed - an insight only reads, which is what makes it safe to point at anything.

It depends on nothing. When strong::BusManager:: is installed alongside it, the bus can be a name, and the insight follows that name from then on - see link::#Buses by name::. When strong::ServerView:: is installed, its meter section grows a button that opens an insight on the main out.

subsection:: What it measures

list::
## strong::spectrum:: - log frequency, the peak in each of 128 bands, with three traces: now, a moment ago, and the loudest in each band since reset.
## strong::levels:: - true peak (ITU-R BS.1770, four times oversampled), sample peak and rms per channel, each holding its highest value until reset.
## strong::loudness:: - momentary (400 ms), short term (3 s), integrated and loudness range, K-weighted and gated as BS.1770 and EBU R128 / Tech 3342 spell out.
## strong::image:: - a goniometer of the stereo pair, with correlation, balance and width.
::

A hint bar along the bottom of the window says what each control does and, for the meters, exactly what each reading measures - hover the code::I:: number, code::TP::, or the goniometer.

subsection:: Buses by name

With link::Classes/BusManager:: installed, the bus can be a Symbol:

code::
BusManager.add(\reverb, 2);
Insight(\verb, \reverb);       // follows the name from now on
Insight.at(\verb).bus_(\out3_4);
::

An insight set to a name follows it: when the bus behind it moves - which it does when the server reboots - the insight goes with it. Setting the bus to a plain index unbinds it again. A name that resolves to nothing changes nothing, unless there is no bus yet, in which case the name is kept and waited for.

subsection:: Running

The analysis is one synth and the language reading its replies, a few messages a second. It is off until something asks for it: opening the window starts it, closing the window stops it again, unless it was already running.

code::
i = Insight.at(\main);
i.run;
i.loudness.integrated;         // LUFS since reset
i.maxTruePeakDb;               // the highest true peak, dBTP
i.reset;                       // integrate again, drop every held maximum
i.stop;
::

subsection:: Server restarts

The analysis registers with code::ServerBoot::, code::ServerTree:: and code::ServerQuit::. A boot takes every node and buffer; the synth and its buffers are made again on the tree hook, and an insight following a name looks its bus up again. cmd + period rebuilds the synth. A quit leaves the picture quiet.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Make an insight under a name, replacing any insight already under that name (its synth and window are freed first).
ARGUMENT:: name
a Symbol. The insight is registered under it and found again with link::#*at::.
ARGUMENT:: bus
what to analyse: an Integer (a bus index), a link::Classes/Bus::, a Symbol (a BusManager name to follow), or a module (its code::tapBus:: is read).
ARGUMENT:: channels
how many channels to analyse, from the start of the bus. Taken from the Bus or the named entry when they say; 2 by default.
ARGUMENT:: server
the link::Classes/Server::. code::Server.default:: unless given.
RETURNS:: the Insight.

METHOD:: at
The insight registered under a name, or nil.
RETURNS:: an Insight.

METHOD:: names
Every insight's name, sorted.

METHOD:: all
The registry: name to Insight.

METHOD:: main
The insight on the main out, bus 0, two channels - made the first time it is asked for.
RETURNS:: an Insight.

METHOD:: open
The main out, window and all: makes link::#*main:: if needed and opens its window. What the ServerView button calls.
RETURNS:: an Insight.

METHOD:: gui
Open the window of the named insight, making the main-out insight if the name is unknown and nothing is there.

METHOD:: freeAll
Free every insight.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

private:: prGuiClosed, update, init, prResolve, prSetBus, prUpdateRegistryLink, prBusMoved, prChannelsChanged, prResetArrays, prResetLive, prRestartNodes, prStart, prStopNodes, prStopPolling, prStartResponders, prFreeResponders, prLevels, prLoud, prStartPoller, prPoll, prGetnMsgs, prChunk, prEnsureSetup, prRemoveHooks, prOnBoot, prOnTree, prOnQuit

METHOD:: bus
The index of the bus being read, or nil while a name is unknown. Setting it takes an index, a link::Classes/Bus::, a BusManager name, or a module - the same as link::#*new::'s code::bus::.

METHOD:: busName
The BusManager name the insight is following, or nil when it is on a bare index.

METHOD:: busLabel
What the window shows: the name followed, or the index, or code::"?"::.

METHOD:: channels
How many channels are analysed. Setting it rebuilds the synth.

METHOD:: run
Start the analysis synth.

METHOD:: stop
Stop it.

METHOD:: running
Whether it has been asked to run.

METHOD:: isAlive
Whether the synth is up and its replies are arriving.

METHOD:: reset
Integrate again from now, and drop every held maximum: the loudness statistics, the highest peaks, the over count, the spectrum's held trace and the history.

METHOD:: loudness
The link::Classes/InsightLoudness:: - momentary, short term, integrated, range.

METHOD:: spectrum
The link::Classes/InsightSpectrum:: - the bands, and the falling traces.

METHOD:: peaks
METHOD:: truePeaks
METHOD:: rms
Amplitude per channel from the last reply: the sample peak, the true peak, and the rms.

METHOD:: maxPeaks
METHOD:: maxTruePeaks
The highest per channel since reset, as amplitudes.

METHOD:: maxTruePeakDb
METHOD:: maxPeakDb
The highest of any channel since reset, in dB.

METHOD:: overs
How many times a true peak has crossed the ceiling since reset.

METHOD:: correlation
The interchannel correlation of the first pair, -1 (out of phase) to +1 (mono).

METHOD:: width
The stereo width: 0 is mono, 1 is fully spread, more than 1 is out of phase.

METHOD:: balance
Left to right, -1 to +1, from the rms of the two channels.

METHOD:: history
The short term loudness of the last link::#-historySeconds:: seconds, one value per 100 ms block.

METHOD:: fftSize
The FFT size, one of code::Insight.fftSizes::. Setting it rebuilds the synth and the spectrum.

METHOD:: source
What the spectrum is of: code::\sum::, code::\left::, code::\right::, code::\mid:: or code::\side::.

METHOD:: tilt
dB per octave added to the drawn spectrum, so pink noise reads flat at 3. A display setting.

METHOD:: smoothing
How much the spectrum is averaged over time, 0 to 0.95.

METHOD:: hold
Whether to keep the loudest-per-band trace.

METHOD:: spectrumFloor
The bottom of the spectrum's dB scale.

METHOD:: target
The loudness aimed at, in LUFS: drawn across the loudness bars and the history. A mark, not a limit.

METHOD:: ceiling
The true peak level, in dBTP, past which a reading is an over. A mark, not a limiter.

METHOD:: historySeconds
How many seconds of short term loudness the history keeps.

METHOD:: imagerFrames
How many frames the goniometer shows at once.

METHOD:: gui
Open, or bring to the front, this insight's window.
RETURNS:: an InsightGUI.

METHOD:: free
Stop the analysis, close the window, and take the insight out of the registry.


EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;

// point it at the main out and watch
Insight.open;

// something to look at
(
x = { Splay.ar(SinOsc.ar([220, 440, 660, 990] * LFNoise0.kr(2).range(1, 1.02), 0, 0.1)) }.play;
)

// read it in code
i = Insight.at(\main);
i.loudness.integrated;
i.maxTruePeakDb;
i.correlation;

i.target = -14;      // aim for -14 LUFS
i.reset;             // start the integration over

x.free;
Insight.freeAll;
::
